        {
          "subject_code": "AY2026",
          "name": "27 Objectives: • To provide hands-on experience on various basic engineering practices in Electrical Engineering. • To provide hands-on experience on various basic engineering practices in Electronics Engineering. • To provide hands-on experience on trouble shooting and software installation List of Experiments A. ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING PRACTICES (20 Hours) 1. Study of power tools 2. Residential house wiring using switches, fuses, indicators, lamp and energy meter. 3. Fluorescent lamp wiring. 4. Stair case wiring. 5. Measurement of electrical quantities - voltage, current, power & power factor in RL circuit. 6. Measurement of earth resistance using Megger. 7. Study of Ceiling Fan and Iron Box 8. Study of Air conditioning B. ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING PRACTICES (20 Hours) 1. Study of electronic components and equipment - Resistor, colour coding, measurement of AC signal parameters (peak-peak, rms period, frequency) using CRO/DSO. 2. (a) Measurement of electrical quantities using Multimeter (b) Testing of electronic components. 3. Study of logic gates: AND, OR, EXOR and NOT. 4. Generation of Clock Signals. 5. Soldering practice - Components Devices and Circuits - Using general purpose PCB. 6. Measurement of ripple factor of Half-wave and Full-wave Rectifiers. C. COMPUTER SYSTEMS PRACTICES (20 Hours) 1. Assembling of Desktop computer 2. Installation of Operating system 3. Installation of application software 4. Disc Partition 5. Trouble shooting - PC & Hand held devices",
          "credits": 5,
          "course_type": "Professional Core",
